Finnish Cultural Etiquette

Social Norms:
- Punctuality is highly valued
- Personal space is important
- Sauna is sacred (nudity common in single-gender saunas)

Key Phrases:
- Kiitos = Thank you
- Hei = Hello
- Anteeksi = Excuse me

Dining Customs:
- Remove shoes in homes
- Wait for host to say "hyvää ruokahalua" (good appetite)
- Coffee is served frequently

Unique Concepts:
- Sisu = Persistence against adversity
- Kalsarikännit = "Pantsdrunk" (drinking at home in underwear)
